/**
 * @mainpage E-Countdown Firmware Project
 * 
 * Target of this project is to create a firmware for a small battery driven
 * which provides date information as well as a countdown (in days) until
 * a event day defined by the client via Bluetooth LE.
 * 
 * The device also provides multiple customization options. The background
 * can be customized by any image content. Font family, style and size are
 * customizable, too. The device contains multiple fonts to choose.
 * 
 * A Fuel Gauge provides battery data which are presented on the display
 * and via bluetooth interface.
 * 
 * Besides the actual firmware this project also contains a display driver component
 * for the [Waveshare 4.26inch e-paper Display](https://www.waveshare.com/product/displays/e-paper/epaper-2/4.26inch-e-paper.htm).
 * 
 * @subpage firmware_page "E-Countdown firmware"
 * 
 * @subpage display_driver_page "Display driver Component"
 */

/**
 * @page firmware_page E-Countdown Firmware
 * 
 * ### Architecture
 * 
 * This firmware is split into 3 tasks:
 * - Main Task (see @ref main.c)
 *   - Initialize hardware and other tasks (see also @ref battery.h, @ref bt.h)
 *   - Handles drawing and display (see also @ref display.h, @ref draw.h)
 *   - Handles Image Storage (see also @ref settings.h, @ref draw.h)
 * - Battery Task (@ref battery.h, @ref battery.c)
 *   - Handles Fuel Gauge interrupts
 *   - Updates battery related infos
 * - Bluetooth LE (@ref bt.h, @ref bt.c)
 *   - Handles GATT server
 *   - Handles Settings Storage (see also @ref settings.h)
 * 
 * After initialization is completed the main thread is suspended.
 * It is for the other tasks to wakeup the main task if the display
 * content needs to be refreshed.
 * 
 * @mermaid
 * sequenceDiagram
 * 	participant MAIN as Main Thread
 * 	participant BAT as Battery Thread
 * 	participant BLE as BLE Thread
 * 
 * 	activate MAIN
 * 	MAIN->>MAIN: Initialize hardware
 * 	MAIN->>BLE: Initialize
 * 	activate BLE
 * 	MAIN->>BAT: Initialize
 * 	activate BAT
 * 	MAIN->>MAIN: Initialize display & drawing logic
 * 	deactivate MAIN
 * 
 * 	BAT->>MAIN: New Battery data
 * 	activate MAIN
 * 	MAIN->>MAIN: Refresh display content
 * 	deactivate MAIN
 * 
 * 	BLE->>MAIN: New client data
 * 	activate MAIN
 * 	MAIN->>MAIN: Refresh display content
 * 	deactivate MAIN
 * 	deactivate BAT
 * 	deactivate BLE
 * @endmermaid
 */

/**
 * @page display_driver_page Display Driver Component
 * 
 * - Header File: @ref epd4in26.h
 * - Implementation: @ref epd4in26.c
 * 
 * ### Main Functions
 * 
 * The display driver is setup as an ESP LCD panel driver.
 * Use @ref esp_lcd_new_panel_epd4in26() to create a driver instance.
 * 
 * ### Extra Functions
 * 
 * This driver extends the default ESP LCD driver interface by 2 further functions.
 * 
 * - @ref epd4in26_gen_test(): Refresh the display with a test image (see @ref epd4in26_test_id_t)
 * - @ref epd4in26_refresh(): Trigger a display refresh
 * 
 * ### Driver Configuration Options
 * 
 * The driver offers some build time configurations found in @ref epd4in26.c.
 * 
 * The driver's pixel format can be configured by setting one of these:
 * - @ref DSP_BPP_1: Display converts images to 1BPP
 * - @ref DSP_BPP_2: Display converts images to 2BPP
 * 
 * It is also possible to configure the dithering algorithm:
 * - @ref DITHER_ALGO_SL: Sierra Lite Dithering
 * - @ref DITHER_ALGO_JJN: Jarvis, Judice and Ninke Dithering
 */